{
  "text": [
    "Amygdalin (Figure 1 ) is a major component of apricot kernels, bitter almonds and peach, plum, pear and apple seeds  .",
    "The amount of cyanogenic glycosides in plants varies with plant species and environmental effects [10] .",
    "For example, apricot seeds and bitter almonds contain approximately 20-80 \u03bcmol/g and 100 \u03bcmol/g of amygdalin, respectively."
  ],
